# General Rules

## TypeScript
- `strict: true`; never `any` — use `unknown` and narrow.
- Explicit function signatures and return types on exported functions.
- Validate external/canonical JSON shape before trusting it (seed time especially).

## Naming
- Files: kebab-case (`mp-card.tsx`, `score-gauge.tsx`, `cohort.ts`).
- Components/Types: PascalCase. Functions/vars: camelCase. Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
- No redundant namespace prefixes (a file in `components/mp/` is `card.tsx`-style domain, not `MpMpCard`).

## Comments
- None. Code is self-documenting. No TODO/FIXME/BUG — open a GitHub issue.
- If a value needs explaining, name it (`CRIMINAL_DEDUCTION_CAP`), don't comment it.

## DRY & structure
- One home per constant: `lib/sources.ts`, `lib/format/scoring.ts`, `lib/schema-constants.ts`, `pipeline/lib/text.ts`.
- No magic numbers; extract to SCREAMING_CASE constants at module top.
- Split files over ~150 lines; single responsibility.
- Reuse `lib/` helpers; never copy-paste utilities between app and pipeline — share via `lib/`.

## Imports
- App/components: `@/...` alias (maps to repo root).
- Pipeline/seed: relative imports with explicit `.ts` extensions (tsx requirement).
- Group: react/next → @/lib & @/components → relative. Blank line between groups.

## Async & errors
- async/await only; no `.then()` chains. Wrap fetch/parse in try/catch with context; never silent-fail.
- `Promise.all` for independent concurrent work.
